[gd_scene load_steps=8 format=3 uid="uid://dealcan0sfgd"]

; BTN-1 (2026-09-19) — ONE OF THE RACK'S THREE NEAR-MISSES: the can.
;
; PLACEHOLDER. Read DealBox.tscn's header for the contract SHELF-1 inherits (same colour, same
; size class, shape apart; these three filenames are the only names anything knows).
;
; THE COLLIDER IS A BOX AROUND A CYLINDER, DELIBERATELY. Godot's CylinderShape3D is the one
; primitive its 3D solver is known to be least happy with, and this prop's whole job is to be SET
; DOWN and STAY there — REACH-1's rest audit fires on every settle and its correction path is
; judged on the collider, so a shape that jitters at rest would turn a level fact into a physics
; argument. A 0.11 x 0.2 x 0.11 box is within 1.6 cm of the can's silhouette everywhere, which is
; well inside what a placeholder owes. SHELF-1 may change it the moment it has a real mesh; if it
; does, the thing to watch is `[props] rest not good` lines in a server log.
;
; The mesh is still a cylinder, because the SHAPE is the mechanic: a seeker glancing at the shelf
; has to be able to say "it was the round one".

